*FQ1-A0*: There were a lot of options for components/doors of which I sometimes what confused which door was the correct one to choose. But could've been on purpose to have choices.

*FQ1-A1*: I often had to double-click on an object, like a button or an edge, in order to activate it or change its properties.

*FQ1-A2*: No Enter to get from Node Name to Description, No Shift + Enter in Node Description to confirm Node and add it

*FQ1-A3*: I didn't see where I could add locks

*FQ1-A4*: I was to dumb to figure out how to add a key, also the right click context actions could be more consistent

*FQ1-A5*: At first it was unclear how to add components (enemies, keys) since editing the node doesnt work, the little dropdown arrow needs to be used. Adding doors etc to edges was confusing at first. For the small map from these tasks, laying out nodes was acceptable, but already slightly frustrating (avoiding overlap, making space for new nodes, ...).

*FQ1-A6*: let me submit the strings with enter, I dont like switching back to the mouse when I am currently tipping

*FQ1-A7*: HOW ON EARTH DO I DELETE EDGES??? Right click needs to do that (if it's not a bug)

*FQ1-A8*: I was a little confused on where to change the edges as in the rooms it was on the nodes but on the edges it was up top, and i didn't get at the start that the only way of deleting edges is using the delete key while everything else is always graphical interface supported

*FQ1-A9*: No multi-select via drop-clicking was frustrating. Also didn't notice lock option on edges until the end. "Key" button for bombs too.

*FQ1-A10*: Adding locks to edges is triggered with a separate menu, which did not pop up by clicking at the edge, having a less natural flow as for the rooms, where edit options where shown in the room box directly.

*FQ1-A11*: When you type into the text and click enter it gives a new line instead of finishing. + Door errors confusing

*FQ1-A12*: The button for adding keys is not in the right-click menu.

*FQ1-A13*: The distinction of which elements classified as 'key' or as 'component' (i.e. enemy vs bomb) was confusing at first

*FQ1-A14*: Adding the Edges

*FQ1-A15*: There could be more information e.g. in tooltips

*FQ1-A16*: Sometimes, when adding a new component, the system was showing weird values in their place, taking roughly a second to update. Also, when clicking on an edge, I wanted to know what kind of lock it showed.

*FQ1-A17*: Locks were a bit weird to set up, the two buttons in the top left felt not quite in place. Also some features have right click context menu actions while others don't.

*FQ1-A18*: When I entered a component wrongly I couldn't change it's value inside the graph window.

*FQ1-A19*: No clear way to edit/remove edges, no clear feedback on editing history

*FQ1-A20*: Deleting did not work with Del button; while keeping additional buttons hidden by default makes the interface sleek, it took me a while to figure out how to place a lock. Having this option available at all times and simply drag&drop it on the corresponding edge would have been more intuitive for me.

*FQ1-A21*: It did not work as "responsive" as i would have liked it at certain points, e.g.  being able to change the edges by double clicking them and so on
